The main cost is in `Field::GetName()` and `GetName(j)`, which return `std::string` by value and allocate on every call. I can't avoid those copies without knowing whether `Field` exposes a `const std::string&` accessor, and I can't add friends or members. So this version keeps the same calls and only trims the loop overhead: it hoists the per-field sub-field count and uses `size_t` indices. The gain is likely small. A bigger win would need a by-reference name accessor on `Field`, which would be a change outside this function.

```cpp
const Field* Mesg::GetField(const std::string& name) const
{
    const size_t count = fields.size();
    for (size_t i = 0; i < count; i++)
    {
        const Field& f = fields[i];
        if (f.GetName() == name)
            return &f;

        const FIT_UINT16 numSub = f.GetNumSubFields();
        for (FIT_UINT16 j = 0; j < numSub; j++)
        {
            if ((f.GetName(j) == name) && CanSupportSubField(&f, j))
                return &f;
        }
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```